  "body": "Under section 6, the spec has a note that begins:\n\n> The user agent's implement may choose to conditionally expose [hid](https://hid.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-hid) attribute of the [Navigator](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/system-state.html#navigator)\n\nThere's a typo here (it should probably start \"The user agent may choose\"), but I'm wondering if we can cover this in a better way anyhow since I'm not sure if notes are normative. Can we instead remove the `ServiceWorker` exposure on the `WorkerNavigator` and `HID` interfaces and instead just describe extension service worker exposure in prose? (I don't have a lot of experience here so I'm not sure what would make the most sense)",
